description:
memory.rs:664-676 in MemoryBackend::update_object expresses 'lookup or return NotFound' as a clone-then-match shape:

```rust
let existing = inner
    .objects_mut(O::TYPE_NAME, account_id.as_ref())
    .get(id)
    .cloned();

let mut current = match existing {
    Some(v) => v,
    None => {
        return Err(BackendSetError::SetError(SetError::new(
            SetErrorType::NotFound,
        )))
    }
};
```

clippy::manual_let_else fires here (and is implied by -W clippy::pedantic). The idiomatic forms are:

(a) let-else:
```rust
let Some(mut current) = inner.objects_mut(O::TYPE_NAME, account_id.as_ref()).get(id).cloned() else {
    return Err(BackendSetError::SetError(SetError::new(SetErrorType::NotFound)));
};
```

(b) ok_or_else + ?:
```rust
let mut current = inner
    .objects_mut(O::TYPE_NAME, account_id.as_ref())
    .get(id)
    .cloned()
    .ok_or_else(|| BackendSetError::SetError(SetError::new(SetErrorType::NotFound)))?;
```

(b) matches the canonical jmap-mail-server shape at crate-jmap-mail-server/src/memory.rs:1049-1051 (.get_mut(id).ok_or_else(...)?). The sharing-server form is wordier and creates a binding (existing) that is only used once on the next line.

Note: the sharing-server's clone-first design is deliberate — bd:JMAP-3t94.13 / JMAP-3t94.19 establish that the patch must NOT mutate stored state on failure, and cloning first gives that atomicity. Both rewrites preserve that property; the change is purely about the bind+match shape.

Workspace-scope: the same match-on-cloned-Option shape appears in 4 sibling MemoryBackends — metadata-server/memory.rs:780, calendars-server/memory.rs:721, contacts-server/memory.rs:660, chat-server/memory.rs:734 — so propagating the fix is a workspace-architectural sweep, not a sharing-server-only cleanup. Canonical jmap-mail-server is the only sibling using the idiomatic form (and uses the get_mut variant that does NOT preserve atomic-on-failure, per its own comment at memory.rs:1053-1057). The sharing-server sweep should adopt form (b) with .cloned() preserved, not form (b) without clone.
